+{
+ "cells": [
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "`Perc` replaces observations with percentile values, computing within each group and recording the requested level in a `percentile` column. By default it returns the endpoints and quartiles (0, 25, 50, 75, and 100), using NumPy's `linear` method.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The `method` parameter accepts NumPy's percentile methods: `inverted_cdf`, `averaged_inverted_cdf`, `closest_observation`, `interpolated_inverted_cdf`, `hazen`, `weibull`, `linear`, `median_unbiased`, `normal_unbiased`, `lower`, `higher`, `midpoint`, and `nearest`. Missing observations are ignored."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {
+    "tags": [
+     "hide"
+    ]
+   },
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import seaborn.objects as so\n",
+    "from seaborn import load_dataset\n",
+    "penguins = load_dataset(\"penguins\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "The default computes quartiles along with the endpoints:"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "so.Plot(penguins, x=\"species\", y=\"body_mass_g\").add(so.Dots(), so.Perc())"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Pass an integer to request a different number of evenly spaced levels:"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "so.Plot(penguins, x=\"species\", y=\"body_mass_g\").add(so.Dots(), so.Perc(11))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Or pass explicit percentile levels:"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "so.Plot(penguins, x=\"species\", y=\"body_mass_g\").add(so.Dots(), so.Perc([10, 50, 90]))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Combine `Perc` with a range mark to show the interquartile interval:"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
